description:
crate-jmap-filenode-server/src/memory.rs:294 — 'let since: u64 = since_state.as_ref().parse().unwrap_or(0);' silently maps an unparseable State token to 0, which means a client sending a corrupt/forged/version-mismatched state gets a fresh-stream-from-the-beginning response rather than the RFC 8620 §5.2-mandated 'cannotCalculateChanges' error.

Cross-walk against the other 6 extension-server siblings (canonical mail-server plus 5 cookie-cut siblings) confirms this is FILENODE-ONLY, NOT canonical-first:

  jmap-chat-server/src/memory.rs:521        .map_err(|_| BackendChangesError::CannotCalculate)?;
  jmap-calendars-server/src/memory.rs:468   .map_err(|_| BackendChangesError::CannotCalculate)?;
  jmap-contacts-server/src/memory.rs:413    .map_err(|_| BackendChangesError::CannotCalculate)?;
  jmap-tasks-server/src/memory.rs:483       .map_err(|_| BackendChangesError::CannotCalculate)?;
  jmap-sharing-server/src/memory.rs:328     .map_err(|_| BackendChangesError::CannotCalculate)?;
  jmap-mail-server/src/memory.rs:543        .map_err(|_| BackendChangesError::Other(MemoryError(...)))  [also wrong shape — returns serverFail instead of cannotCalculateChanges, separate workspace-canonical issue]
  jmap-filenode-server/src/memory.rs:294    .unwrap_or(0);   [this bug]

The prior /review-rusty pass's calibration note cited 'mail-server memory.rs:198 same shape' as justification for deferring this as canonical-first. That cross-reference was wrong: mail-server line 198 is 'rfc3339_to_epoch_secs(...).unwrap_or(0)' on a Thread receivedAt sort key, an entirely different shape and call site. Mail-server's actual since_state.parse() at line 543 does map_err (albeit to the wrong variant; that is a separate canonical-first finding).

Fix is filenode-only:
    let since: u64 = since_state.as_ref().parse().map_err(|_| {
        BackendChangesError::CannotCalculate
    })?;

Idiom category: error-handling — a silent unwrap_or fallback on a parse where the caller-meaningful error is well-defined and supported by the workspace's existing typed error enum.

Note: BackendChangesError variants need a quick re-confirm that ::CannotCalculate is the right variant for filenode-server (its Other(Self::Error) variant exists but is wrong for this case).
